ticularly concerning in patients with specific health conditions, such as gastroesophageal reflux disease, where it may indicate potential complications, and in cancer patients, where it is commonly associated with malnutrition and caquexia.\n\nIn geriatric patients, weight loss can also signify malnutrition and is a common symptom that necessitates further investigation. The assessment of weight loss is crucial in various medical contexts, including the management of patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (EPOC), where it may relate to malnutrition and increased energy expenditure. Additionally, weight loss is a monitored outcome in neonates, especially regarding fluid management and overall health assessment.\n\nOverall, \"\"PÉRDIDA DE PESO\"\" is a significant health concern that is systematically measured and classified according to its severity, serving as a vital parameter in diagnosing malnutrition and assessing the overall health status of patients across different medical conditions.\",27\r\n2093,CIRUGÍA,\"CIRUGÍA refers to surgical procedures that encompass a range of medical interventions, particularly significant in the context of patient care and recovery. These procedures often necessitate nutritional support, as they can lead to alterations in the nutritional status of patients, especially those with cancer, resulting in weight loss and potential complications. The surgical department is responsible for the comprehensive care and treatment of patients, which includes the administration of parenteral nutrition and the placement of enteral feeding tubes to ensure adequate nutritional intake.\n\nMoreover, surgery can impact critical health markers such as albumin levels and overall nutritional status, particularly in critically ill patients. It is also noted that surgical procedures may induce insulin resistance and hyperglycemia, which can further complicate recovery and affect patient outcomes. In specific cases, such as surgeries involving head and neck cancer patients, immunomodulatory formulas may be utilized to support recovery. Therefore, careful nutritional considerations are essential both before and after surgical interventions to optimize patient health and recovery outcomes.\",11\r\n556,RIESGO NUTRICIONAL,\"RIESGO NUTRICIONAL refers to the potential for malnutrition or adverse health outcomes resulting from inadequate nutritional intake or status. This concern is particularly significant for patients undergoing bariatric surgery, as they may experience malabsorption, which can exacerbate nutritional deficiencies. Additionally, nutritional risk encompasses the possibility that patients, especially those with conditions such as cancer, may not receive sufficient nutrients. Various screening tools are utilized to assess this risk, ensuring that patients are monitored for potential malnutrition and its associated health implications.\",4\r\n7301,CÁNCER DE ESÓFAGO,\"Cáncer de esófago es una enfermedad que afecta el esófago, caracterizada por la formación de células malignas en sus tejidos. Esta neoplasia se asocia con una alta incidencia de malnutrición y pérdida de peso en los pacientes, lo que puede llevar a complicaciones graves como la caquexia. A menudo, el cáncer de esófago es diagnosticado en estadios avanzados y presenta síntomas como disfagia, que es la dificultad para tragar. El tratamiento de esta enfermedad generalmente requiere un enfoque quirúrgico, como la esofagectomía, así como un manejo nutricional especializado para abordar las complicaciones relacionadas con la malnutrición. Además, se ha observado que un mayor consumo de frutas y verduras puede reducir el riesgo de desarrollar carcinoma epidermoide, una de las formas más comunes de cáncer de esófago. En resumen, el cáncer de esófago es una condición grave que no solo afecta la salud física del paciente, sino que también requiere un enfoque integral en su tratamiento y manejo nutricional.\",16\r\n2259,CAQUEXIA TUMORAL,\"CAQUEXIA TUMORAL is a syndrome associated with advanced cancer, characterized by hypercatabolism and mediated by inflammatory cytokines. This condition is often irreversible and complicates nutritional treatment for affected patients. It is a multifactorial syndrome that leads to the progressive loss of skeletal muscle in cancer patients, significantly impacting their quality of life and survival rates. Despite its prevalence in oncological patients, there is limited evidence regarding the influence of nutrition on the progression of CAQUEXIA TUMORAL.\",8\r\n13373,INFLAMACIÓN SISTÉMICA,\"La inflamación sistémica es una respuesta del cuerpo que puede ser provocada por el cáncer. Esta condición afecta el metabolismo y puede contribuir a la malnutrición en los pacientes. Además, se ha observado que la inflamación sistémica está relacionada con la pérdida de peso en estos pacientes, lo cual se asocia con niveles elevados de proteína C-reactiva (PCR).\",4\r\n13372,ODINOFAGIA,\"ODINOFAGIA refers to the pain experienced while swallowing, which significantly impacts patients diagnosed with esophageal cancer. This condition complicates the intake of both food and liquids, making it a challenging symptom for those affected. In the context of esophageal cancer, odinofagia is recognized as a common symptom that can severely hinder the quality of life for patients.\",4\r\n12610,AYUNO PREOPERATORIO,\"AYUNO PREOPERATORIO refers to the practice of fasting prior to surgical procedures, which has been developed and refined over time to minimize the risk of complications during surgery. This preoperative fasting is recommended to ensure patient safety and improve surgical outcomes by preventing issues such as aspiration and other related complications.\",4\r\n3433,HOMBRE,\"HOMBRE es un género que se refiere a los varones humanos. En este contexto, se menciona en relación con el gasto energético basal, que es la cantidad mínima de energía que el cuerpo necesita para mantener sus funciones vitales en reposo.\",9\r\n1720,DIFICULTADES PARA ALIMENTARSE,,3\r\n1718,EXPLORACIÓN CLÍNICA,Evaluación física del paciente para determinar el estado de salud y nutrición,1\r\n2278,TRATAMIENTOS,\"Tratamientos refers to the various medical interventions, such as surgery, radiotherapy, and chemotherapy, that can affect the nutritional status and weight of cancer patients.\",1\r\n13386,ESOFAECTOMÍA,,1\r\n13374,AUMENTO DEL GASTO ENERGÉTICO,\"Condición que contribuye a la pérdida de peso en pacientes con cáncer, relacionada con la caquexia tumoral.\",1\r\n12611,ANESTESIA,\"Anesthesia is a medical intervention used during surgery to prevent pain and awareness, influencing preoperative fasting guidelines.\",1\r\n1717,ACTIVIDAD COTIDIANA,Descripción de la actividad diaria del paciente en el último mes,1\r\n1716,ALIMENTACIÓN RESPECTO HACE 1 MES,Evaluación de los cambios en la alimentación del paciente en el último mes,1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3301,PACIENTE,PÉRDIDA DE PESO,\"The patient experienced significant weight loss, which was a critical indicator of their health status. This weight loss contributed to the patient's state of malnutrition, as it was primarily due to reduced food intake. The significant loss of weight was particularly noted during their hospital stay, highlighting the severity of the patient's condition.\",573\r\n3089,PACIENTE,CIRUGÍA,\"El servicio de Cirugía está a cargo del tratamiento y manejo del paciente con pancreatitis aguda. Además, un paciente puede necesitar soporte nutricional antes y después de una cirugía para asegurar una recuperación adecuada.\",557\r\n3035,PACIENTE,RIESGO NUTRICIONAL,\"The entity \"\"PACIENTE\"\" is evaluated for \"\"RIESGO NUTRICIONAL\"\" to assess nutritional risk, which helps determine the potential need for intervention. This assessment is crucial in identifying patients who may require additional nutritional support or intervention based on their ri